'''Ancient Egg: N203''' is a [[:Category:Special Cats|Special Cat]] that can be obtained from the [[June Bride of the Devil (Event Gacha)|June Bride of the Devil]] event. It was added in [[Version 12.4 Update|Version 12.4]].

{{Cat Info
|ID = 713
|rarity = EX
|name1 = Ancient Egg: N203
|name2 = Violet Egg: N203
|name3 = Clown Cat
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Violet Egg: N203''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Clown Cat''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit#Behemoth Stones|Behemoth Stones]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
==='''Normal/Evolved Form'''===
These forms are <u>useless by design</u>. Similarly to the other [[:Category:Ancient Eggs|Ancient Eggs]], this unit is not meant to be used before its True Form. However, due to its somewhat low cost and quick recharge, it may be used as an emergency meatshield in [[Underground Labyrinth]] or [[Legend Quest]] if you have no use for its True Form.

==='''True Form'''===
Clown Cat can be used like an anti-Zombie [[Cat Gunslinger (Rare Cat)|Cat Gunslinger]]. Just like Gunslinger, despite having a low slow chance, they can be stacked to slow their targeted trait with decent effectiveness. The problem with this unit is that slow against Zombies isn't great, due to it not being able to prevent zombies from burrowing. In addition, if a Zombie burrows into Clown Cat's range, Clown Cat will likely die due to their unimpressive health and DPS. You're going to be better off using units like [[Gardener Cat (Rare Cat)|Gardener]] or [[Welterweight Cat (Rare Cat)|Welterweight Cat]] for crowd controlling Zombies.

With that being said, there isn't really any reason not to use Clown Cat along with other Zombie crowd controllers such as [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Vaulter Cat]], which they have great synergy with due to them being able to cover Vaulter's blindspot. It is also worth mentioning that they have [[Soulstrike]]. While this may sound good, Soulstrike actually hurts Clown Cat as a unit since stopping in front of a corpse means that they're not attacking other units that could be affected by their crowd control. Clown also has horrid DPS, meaning that they'll struggle to kill enemy corpses anyway. Their behemoth slayer can be outright ignored since there are very few zombie behemoths, and it stands no chance against those few. Overall, Clown Cat can be used in many early game Zombie stages, but becomes obsolete late game as Zombies that outrange it become more prevalent and superior Zombie crowd controllers are unlocked.

